+++ b/docs/target-spool-format.md
@@ -1,3 +1,13 @@
 # Target spool format
 
-TBD.
+The FRAMING is binary: `RUN_MAGIC`, then length-framed records (u32
+big-endian length prefix + record bytes), ending in a record-count +
+SHA-256 footer computed over the framed stream.
+
+Each record PAYLOAD inside a frame is serde_json — deliberately not a
+packed binary codec. The protobuf bar bytes therefore serialize as a JSON
+integer array (a ~3-4x size blow-up per bar). That trade is intentional:
+this spool serves only the small target-only population, where JSON
+debuggability wins and verbosity is harmless. Do NOT reuse this writer for
+full-population canonical loads; size scratch from JSON record sizes, not
+raw protobuf sizes.
